                                          Practice Hypothesis Development

You will be tasked with writing hypotheses based on relevant intelligence provided to you. There are three steps to
the hypothesis development process:

. 1. State your hypothesis - write a clear and concise hypothesis statement that contain all necessary detail.
The tense used in your writing is important, past tense is the correct way to convey a hypothesis statement
(e.g. may have ... ).

. 2. State what data sources(s) does your hypothesis rely on - using the provided Technique ID related to your
hypothesis, research and provide the data source(s) (Event codes and Event IDs) that would allow an analyst
to prove or disprove your hypothesis. Ensure you provide a description of the data source(s).
o Sysmon event code 1 and windows event ID 4688 should always be provided as relevant data
source(s).
o MITRE ATT&CK should be used as a primary method of research for identifying data source(s) and for
identifying indicators commonly used in the associated technique(s).

. 3. Provide indicators you expect to find during the hunt execution that will act as evidence to support your
hypothesis. Copy the event codes and event IDs found in step two and add relevant field names to those
data source(s). Then, using the same source of those event codes, research and report three relevant
indicators per hypothesis in the correct fields, these should be treated as active Kibana queries.
o Example: Event.code: 1 and Process.executable: *process.exe*
